arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-eb3c2d2ab48d449692897822df76ab7f/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

The project structure:
- `ShipmentTracker/` - server project
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` - client project (interactive components go here)

## Requirements
- Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
- Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
- Interactive Auto global mode (components run on server first visit, WebAssembly after)
- Authentication with Individual accounts (already scaffolded)

## What to implement

### 1. Remove template pages
Delete these files from `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`:
- `Counter.razor`
- `Weather.razor`
Keep `Home.razor`, `Auth.razor`, and `NotFound.razor` (we'll modify Home).

### 2. Create shared models in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/`

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 3. Create service interface in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string email);
    Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 4. Create client-side implementation in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string email)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(email)}") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        await _http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
    }
}
```

### 5. Register HttpClient and service in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs`:
Replace the contents with:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>(client =>
{
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress);
});

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

Wait — `AddHttpClient` is not available in WebAssembly. Use `AddScoped` with a factory instead:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress) });
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### 6. Create server-side implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServerService.cs`:
```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentServerService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly ApplicationDbContext _db;

    public ShipmentServerService(ApplicationDbContext db)
    {
        _db = db;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string email)
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.Where(s => s.CustomerEmail == email).OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var shipment = await _db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
        if (shipment is not null)
        {
            shipment.Status = status;
            if (status == ShipmentStatus.Delivered)
                shipment.ActualDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow;
            await _db.SaveChangesAsync();
        }
    }
}
```

### 7. Add Shipment entity to the DbContext

Edit `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` — add a `DbSet<Shipment>` property:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options) : IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>(options)
{
    public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
}
```

### 8. Create API endpoints

Create `ShipmentTracker/Endpoints/ShipmentEndpoints.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Endpoints;

public static class ShipmentEndpoints
{
    public static void MapShipmentEndpoints(this WebApplication app)
    {
        var group = app.MapGroup("api/shipments");

        group.MapGet("/", async (IShipmentService service) =>
            await service.GetAllShipmentsAsync())
            .RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapGet("/track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var shipment = await service.GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(trackingNumber);
            return shipment is not null ? Results.Ok(shipment) : Results.NotFound();
        }).RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapGet("/customer/{email}", async (string email, IShipmentService service) =>
            await service.GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(email))
            .RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapPut("/{id}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatus status, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            await service.UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(id, status);
            return Results.NoContent();
        }).RequireAuthorization();
    }
}
```

### 9. Update server `Program.cs`

Add these registrations and endpoint mapping. Add after the `AddSingleton<IEmailSender...>` line:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServerService>();
```
Add the using statements at the top:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Endpoints;
```
Add before `app.Run();`:
```csharp
app.MapShipmentEndpoints();
```

### 10. Create pages in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`

**Replace `Home.razor` with:**
```razor
@page "/"

<PageTitle>ShipmentTracker - Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Welcome to ShipmentTracker</h1>
<p class="lead">Track and manage your shipments in real time.</p>

<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <div class="row mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5 class="card-title">My Shipments</h5>
                        <p class="card-text">View the status and estimated delivery of your shipments.</p>
                        <a href="track" class="btn btn-primary">Track Shipments</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5 class="card-title">Dispatch Dashboard</h5>
                        <p class="card-text">View all shipments, update statuses, and manage deliveries.</p>
                        <a href="dispatch" class="btn btn-secondary">Open Dashboard</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </Authorized>
    <NotAuthorized>
        <p class="mt-3">Please <a href="Account/Login">log in</a> or <a href="Account/Register">register</a> to track your shipments.</p>
    </NotAuthorized>
</AuthorizeView>
```

**Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Dispatch.razor`:**
```razor
@page "/dispatch"
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.Authorize]
